1
00:04:56,666 --> 00:05:02,666
Some girls would kill to be Cheerleaders.

2
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:59,333
Cheerleader Camp is a comedy, horror, thriller film directed by John Quinn.

3
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:56,000
A cheerleader named Alison is plagued by nightmares about the upcoming all-state
finals and attends a summer training camp with her teammates.

4
00:19:46,666 --> 00:19:52,666
When a number of deaths start occurring at the camp, Alison's nightmares turn twisted and
brutal, and she begins to believe that she may be responsible for the mayhem.

5
00:24:43,333 --> 00:24:49,333
Alison Wentworth, played by Betsy Russell.

6
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Brent Hoover, played by Leif Garrett.

7
00:34:36,666 --> 00:34:42,666
Cory Foster, played by Lucinda Dickey.

8
00:39:33,333 --> 00:39:39,333
Bonnie Reed, played by Lorie Griffin.

9
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Pop, played by George Buck Flower.

10
00:49:26,666 --> 00:49:32,666
Pamela Bently, played by Teri Weigel.

11
00:54:23,333 --> 00:54:29,333
Cheerleader Camp is a 1988 American slasher film produced and directed by John Quinn in his
directorial debut, and starring Betsy Russell, Leif Garrett, Lucinda Dickey, and Lorie Griffin.

12
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
The film follows a troubled young woman who arrives at a cheerleader summer
camp for a competition, where a series of murders begin to occur.

13
01:04:16,666 --> 01:04:22,666
Production of Cheerleader Camp began in 1987.

14
01:09:13,333 --> 01:09:19,333
It was originally intended to be filmed in Oregon, but was instead shot largely
in Camp Nelson, California, and in the Sequoia National Forest.

15
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:16,000
The film was given a brief theatrical release in early 1988 under the title Bloody Pom
Poms before Prism Entertainment released it on video in November 1988.

16
01:19:06,666 --> 01:19:12,666
The film explores themes of nightmare, summer camp, cheerleader, mascot, bikini.

17
01:24:03,333 --> 01:24:09,333
The tone is intense and lighthearted and dark.
